</section>
<section aria-labelledby="switch-h">
  <h2 id="switch-h" class="type-h2">Theme switch</h2>
  <p>A segmented Light | Dark control for blue surfaces such as a footer or menu overlay. It is two native radio buttons, so the arrow keys work without a script.</p>
  {% demo "Theme switch", "brand" %}
  {% set themeSwitchName = "theme-demo" %}{% include "theme-switch.njk" %}
  {% enddemo %}
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="how-h">
  <h2 id="how-h" class="type-h2">How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>A small script in the page head reads a saved choice and sets <code>data-theme</code> on the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element before the page paints, so there is no flash.</li>
    <li>With no saved choice, the page follows the browser through <code>prefers-color-scheme</code>.</li>
    <li>Clicking a control saves the choice in <code>localStorage</code>. Storage can be blocked, so the theme still applies for the visit if it is.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
